              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioners (Solicitor General Paul D. Clement), according to Petitioners (Solicitor General Paul D. Clement), the petitioners argue that taxpayer standing is limited to narrow circumstances identified in Flast, and that broader standing would be overbroad."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "GENERAL CLEMENT",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "a86e03f7916da729be4a29a7597f3e75709d5a0681ace114d5ef000ed00a600a",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-a86e03f7916d-0003-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 59,
                "start": 59
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to GENERAL CLEMENT, even if taxpayer standing is denied, the petitioners note that other directly injured parties could still bring suits."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner Position",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Andrew J. Pincus",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "a86e03f7916da729be4a29a7597f3e75709d5a0681ace114d5ef000ed00a600a",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-a86e03f7916d-0001-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 31,
                "start": 30
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Andrew J. Pincus, respondents contend that to establish standing, a taxpayer must point to a discrete, non\u2011incidental expenditure, not merely a general grant."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "MR. PINCUS",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "a86e03f7916da729be4a29a7597f3e75709d5a0681ace114d5ef000ed00a600a",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-a86e03f7916d-0001-0004"
              ],
