              }
            },
            {
              "document_hash": "a86e03f7916da729be4a29a7597f3e75709d5a0681ace114d5ef000ed00a600a",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-a86e03f7916d-0002-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 38,
                "start": 38
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "They argue that the money must be central to the alleged constitutional violation; the entire grant is unconstitutional because of how the grantees use the funds."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "MR. PINCUS",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "a86e03f7916da729be4a29a7597f3e75709d5a0681ace114d5ef000ed00a600a",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-a86e03f7916d-0003-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 57,
                "start": 57
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to MR. PINCUS, they maintain that the Court has previously required a distinction between taxing/spending and property issues, and that the present grant violates that distinction."
        }
